  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 5.3. Increased capacity of Member States to design and deliver innovative, flexible and inclusive learning options, encompassing work-based learning and quality apprenticeships</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2022-23, under the auspices of the Ministry of Technical and Vocational Education and Training of Yemen, the Social Fund for Development and civil society organizations trained 402 vulnerable youth and women on market-demand-driven skills and occupations and developed or updated six curricula of occupations in demand in Lahj , Abyan , Taiz , Hajjah , Hodieda , almahweet and Saadah. With the support from the European Union and the Swedish International Development Agency, the ILO supported the stakeholders in the development and adaptation of the methodology for apprenticeship, supervision of the quality of training of master training, work-based training, and assessment, thereby enabling them for job placement. The ILO strengthened the capacity of the stakeholders to expand and use the ILO apprenticeship scheme .</narrative>
   </description>
